\date{2026-11-03T03:22:54Z}
  \title{ICPC}

  \p{I've decided to host a competition site for the [International Collegiate Programming Contest](https://icpc.global/) (ICPC) regional contest on October 31.  We've never been able to do this before, because it required having enough computer lab space for all the teams to have their own computer; we had very little computer lab space when I arrived ten years ago, and even less now. In any case, the University of Arkansas Fort Smith always hosted a site, which we would travel to (about a 2.5-hour drive) every fall.  But this year, Fort Smith dropped off the list of sites—the faculty member who used to organize it seems to have moved on. At the same time, our region is moving to having teams bring their own computers, and handing out bootable USB sticks with a standard image that they are required to use for the contest; so computer lab space is no longer a limiting factor.  We'll see how it goes.  In the next few weeks I need to buy some USB sticks and copy a disk image onto them!}
